<section id="how-it-works" tabindex="-1" class="story-process" aria-labelledby="process-title"><div class="container story-section">
<div class="story-heading" data-reveal><span class="eyebrow">02 / FROM ENERGY DATA TO DECISIONS</span><h2 id="process-title">Forecast demand.<br>Review where to optimize.</h2><p>Start with available energy data, then add forecast context when interval coverage qualifies.</p></div>
<div class="story-data-paths grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2" data-reveal><article><span class="eyebrow">UTILITY BILLS</span><h3>Track energy use and spending.</h3><p>Enter a bill’s period, kWh, and amount. With at least two months, compare changes in consumption and spend. Bill-only records do not produce a demand forecast.</p></article><article><span class="eyebrow">INTERVAL READINGS</span><h3>Understand when demand happens.</h3><p>Upload a <code>timestamp,kwh</code> CSV. Caldren checks timestamps, kWh values, and duplicate timestamps within the file.</p><code class="story-csv">2026-10-01 09:00,42.6</code></article></div>
<div class="story-scene story-scene-reverse" data-scroll-scene><figure class="story-stage"><div class="story-stage-images" aria-hidden="true"><img class="is-active" src="{{ asset('images/context.webp') }}" alt="" loading="lazy" width="1308" height="912" data-scene-image data-story-image data-image-index="0"><img src="{{ asset('images/context (2).webp') }}" alt="" loading="lazy" width="1308" height="912" data-scene-image data-story-image data-image-index="1"><img src="{{ asset('images/context (3).webp') }}" alt="" loading="lazy" width="1308" height="912" data-scene-image data-story-image data-image-index="2"><img src="{{ asset('images/context (4).webp') }}" alt="" loading="lazy" width="1308" height="912" data-scene-image data-story-image data-image-index="3"></div><figcaption><span>ENERGY WORKFLOW</span><strong data-scene-caption>01 / Context</strong></figcaption></figure><div class="story-chapters">
<article data-story-step data-image-index="0" data-caption="01 / Context"><span class="eyebrow">01 / CONTEXT</span><h3>Set up an energy workspace.</h3><p>Create an organization and add each site's location, time zone, standard energy rate, and relevant peak tariff settings. Workspace owners can invite teammates.</p><span class="story-footnote">Organize the sites your energy team is responsible for reviewing.</span></article>
<article data-story-step data-image-index="1" data-caption="02 / History"><span class="eyebrow">02 / HISTORY</span><h3>Bring in energy use and bills.</h3><p>Upload interval readings or record monthly bills for the relevant site. Caldren checks formatting and values before saving. Recent data coverage is checked again when a forecast is requested.</p><span class="story-footnote">Bills show spending trends; interval readings unlock demand estimates when coverage qualifies.</span></article>
<article data-story-step data-image-index="2" data-caption="03 / Forecast"><span class="eyebrow">03 / FORECAST</span><h3>Review a seven-day demand outlook.</h3><p>Forecasts require at least 14 complete days of recent hourly or sub-hourly readings with sufficient daily coverage. Caldren sends bounded daily summaries, a historical baseline, time zone, and tariff settings to the Groq API. Returned estimates are checked against the history.</p><span class="story-footnote">Missing coverage? Add recent readings. Generation unavailable? Your history stays visible and you can retry.</span></article>
<article data-story-step data-image-index="3" data-caption="04 / Optimization review"><span class="eyebrow">04 / OPTIMIZATION REVIEW</span><h3>Decide what merits a closer look.</h3><p>Review possible peak alerts and tariff-aware opportunities with energy, facilities, and finance colleagues. Compare suggestions with actual demand, schedules, and operating constraints before changing operations.</p><span class="story-footnote">Caldren supports human review. It does not control equipment or guarantee savings.</span></article>
</div></div></div></section>
